# SABOTAGE: issue #11 / ADR-048 §6 — the tool DECISION stamp (`decide_tool!/3`) REPLACES the
# turn row's meta with a fresh map instead of merging into it, as it did before #11's
# follow-up. A turn whose Level 2 retry comes back as a TOOL call then loses the
# `context_retries` counter §6 puts "on the same turn row", and the failed attempt's tokens
# stamped beside it — the turn ledger stops explaining the run's bill.
#
# Flips the recovered-tool-turn test. Plain (non-tool) recovered turns stay green: they
# never pass through `decide_tool!/3`, which is why this survived every shipped Level 2 test.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/ai/agent_tools_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: RED: a recovered TOOL turn keeps its context_retries counter and the failed attempt's tokens
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/samen/ai/agent.ex b/samen_core/lib/samen/ai/agent.ex
index 19b9f66..9d040b9 100644
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/ai/agent.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/ai/agent.ex
@@ -3050,8 +3050,8 @@ defmodule Samen.AI.Agent do
     # `context_retries` counter and the failed attempt's tokens are stamped on this row
     # BEFORE the retry, and a retry that comes back as a tool call must not erase them.
     meta =
-      prior
-      |> Map.put("args_digest", digest)
+      # SABOTAGE (#11): the tool stamp REPLACES the row's meta again.
+      %{"args_digest" => digest}
       |> maybe_put_divergent(prior["args_digest"], digest)
 
     turn_row
